# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTHING IN content/ IS COMMITTED.
#
# Not the source material (her teachers' PDFs, scans, photos and slide decks),
# and NOT the generated packs either. The packs quote her teachers' own
# material -- the genetics pack carries 51 instuderingsfrågor verbatim, one of
# which is on the prov -- so a pack is as sensitive as the scan it came from.
#
# Packs are generated on this machine and sent to her phone directly, where the
# app's import screen loads them. The build therefore ships as an empty shell,
# which is what makes it safe to host publicly.
#
# Git history is permanent. See docs/CONTENT_GUIDE.md.
#
# This is an ALLOWLIST, and it allows only the directory markers. A per-file
# exception would be the obvious thing to write and the wrong thing: whatever
# file it named would eventually be overwritten with real material. The test
# suite's own sample pack lives in src/test/ for exactly that reason.
/content/*
!/content/packs/
!/content/assets/
!/content/sources/
content/packs/*
!content/packs/.gitkeep
content/assets/*
!content/assets/.gitkeep
content/sources/*
!content/sources/.gitkeep
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
